  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity building in ethical and legal aspects of AI.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Artificial Intelligence (AI) applications continue to expand opportunities for progress of humankind and the achievement of the Sustainable Development Goals, at the same AI is raising various threats. The 32 Member States which responded to UNESCO survey on AI assessment have underlined the importance of UNESCO&#x2019;s work concerning AI in the fields of education, sciences, culture and communication and information. To anticipate the bad effects of AI on education, UNESCO Liaison Office jointly with the Ministry of Education and the Ministry of Innovation and technology will organize a workshop on the ethical and legal aspects of AI in Education for teachers, researchers as well as for learners.</narrative>
  </description>
